<!--
  Beat 6 of the flagship, on the `Two-Col Evidence` layout.

  A label on the left, a claim on the right, and the headline itself is the demonstration: someone
  who reads only it already has the finding (`assertion-headline`).

  The two boxes are the theme's `Callout` in native shapes — a tinted panel with a coloured edge —
  and the right one takes `accent` because it is the thing to look at, which is the only job
  `accent-is-attention` gives that role. Each is a pair of rectangles rather than one bordered
  shape, because DrawingML has no single-side border and a four-sided one would be a box drawn round
  the evidence for its own sake.

  The prose under each box sits in the layout's pane placeholders, moved down to clear the callout.
  The panes are 544 px on a 48 px gutter, from the layout; nothing here invents a column.
-->
